course: dictionary
lesson: 5432
title: Lakhs and crores
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Big numbers can be said and written in different ways around the world. In India, Pakistan, Bangladesh, Nepal and Sri Lanka, people use the word lakh. One lakh is one hundred thousand, which is 100,000. In Indian writing it is often shown as 1,00,000, with the commas in different places.
explain: The sentence «An adult heart at rest beats roughly 100,000 times a day (a lakh, in Indian English)» gives the same number two ways. The brackets tell you that 100,000 is called a lakh in Indian English. Use the clues around a word to match it to its number.
explain: Ten lakh make one million, and a hundred lakh make one crore. Look for lakh in news from South Asia, such as one lakh rupees or lakhs of people. Lakhs of people means hundreds of thousands of people.
fact: A lakh is one hundred thousand: 100,000.
fact: Ten lakh make one million: 1,000,000.
fact: A hundred lakh make one crore: 10,000,000.
fact: In Indian number writing, 100,000 is written 1,00,000.
fact: Lakh is used in India, Pakistan, Bangladesh, Nepal and Sri Lanka.
exercise: What is one lakh? | 10,000 | 1,000 | 1,000,000 | *100,000
exercise: Ten lakh make one million. Ten lakh is the same as what? | 10,000,000 | 10,000 | 100,000 | *1,000,000
exercise: One crore is a hundred lakh. How is one crore written in digits? | 1,000,000 | 100,000 | 1,00,000 | *10,000,000
test: «An adult heart at rest beats roughly 100,000 times a day.» In Indian English, what is this number called? | Ten lakh | *One lakh | One million | One crore
test: A hundred lakh make one crore. How many is one crore? | 1,000,000,000 | *10,000,000 | 100,000 | 1,000,000
exam: A news report says «lakhs of people» came to the festival. What does lakhs mean here? | Ten people | Exactly 100 people | A few dozen people | *Hundreds of thousands of people
